-Raw coordinates $\mathbf{x}$ and $\mathbf{d}$ are rarely used directly due to the spectral bias of MLPs, which struggle to fit high-frequency details [G]. They are mapped to a higher-dimensional space using positional encoding $\gamma(\cdot)$ [G]. For a coordinate $\mathbf{x}$, the encoding includes the original value and sinusoidal functions at increasing frequencies:
+Methods in this family typically condition a neural network on a latent code to synthesize views, though input dimensions vary (e.g., 6D for position and direction, or 3D for position only) [G]. They employ differentiable volume rendering or feature-based rendering to generate images [G]. Raw coordinates $\mathbf{x}$ and $\mathbf{d}$ are rarely used directly due to the spectral bias of MLPs, which struggle to fit high-frequency details [G]. They are mapped to a higher-dimensional space using positional encoding $\gamma(\cdot)$ [G]. For a coordinate $\mathbf{x}$, the encoding includes the original value and sinusoidal functions at increasing frequencies:
